<title>USA: US Senate chair Cochran backs $500 mln EEP request.</title>
<headline>US Senate chair Cochran backs $500 mln EEP request.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chairman of the Senate Appropriations subcommittee on agriculture said Tuesday he was &quot;inclined&quot; to support a $500 million request for the Export Enhancement Program in fiscal 1998.</p>
<p>Congress allotted $100 million for EEP this year.</p>
<p>&quot;I'm inclined to support what you're asking for,&quot; panel Chairman Thad Cochran, Mississippi Republican, said at a hearing.</p>
<p>Agriculture Department officials say the funding, the maximum allowed under trade rules, would protect U.S. exports from unfair competition.</p>
</text>
